[Music]  after Blade Runner implanted itself into  the minds of moviegoers back in 1982  elements of its cyberpunk world and  story would echo throughout pop culture  for decades to come  despite writers filmmakers and game  designers telling stories in similar  worlds with outstanding results  the familiar dark rainy streets grimy  neon lights and cautionary tales of body  augmentations remained seemingly  steadfast with that in mind it's a small  revelation to see polish studio Bluebird  team take early cues from these  influences and use them as a springboard  to create something new and exciting  with observer you there  yeah I'm a year set in the year 2080 for  observer tells the story of Daniel as  our ski played by blade runner's Rutger  Hauer Lazar ski is a detective who works  the despair ridden streets of Krakow  under the direction of the leading  corporation of the fifth polish Republic  Kyra the world at large has gone to ruin  a digital plague killed thousands of  Augmented people and a colossal war  wiped out any previous global  superpowers thanks to this all-consuming  conflict Chiron rose from the ashes and  became the leading authority and  manufacturer of basically everything  Lazar ski takes jobs from his contact at  Chiron and using his body tech is able  to violently jack into the minds and  memories of people alive or dead to  track clues and solve crimes hence his  official title observer Lazar C gets  called to a slum in the worst part of  Cracow and this is where the majority of  the game takes place talking to  residents examining crime scenes and  deciphering clues make up a lot of the  gameplay here indicating the killer was  in a frenzy but it's all housed inside  gorgeously detailed environments the  twisted memories of deranged strangers  and one of the most intriguing cyberpunk  narratives in years the society that has  been carved out in this apartment  building is all that matters and it's  here that observer starts to pull away  from his influences and blaze its own  unique trail Lazar skis slowly unravels  events with his Augmented technology by  scanning crime scenes for either  biological or electronic evidence he  also makes use of his Dream Eater  augmentation which is designed to  observe people's minds  throughout the course of the game it is  these extraordinary sequences that  present the horrific story beats in  psychedelic and surreal ways from  terrifying nightmare worlds and game  designs that border on mad genius both  you and Lazar ski emerged from these  sessions mentally exhausted but also  instantly compelled to push forward to  find out what happens next  exploration discovery and human  interaction drive the narrative forward  in these bloody crime scenes and filthy  apartments the ability to open a door  inches at a time as another sense of  sweat-soaked tension to the game and  whether it's scanning ID tags and  illegal body mods or sneaking a look at  the tenant list before the janitor comes  back it all pushes you deeper into  observers illusion hallways creak as you  stalk from door to door listening to  bizarre noises rising from each  apartment the crackle of terrified  residents through speakers broken video  screens blasting static and the  cacophony of rain storms envelop you in  an uncomfortable tale mixed with the  truly disturbing sounds coming from  somewhere in the basement and an ominous  industrial soundtrack observers clutches  become almost impossible to escape  [Music]  don't be afraid I'm here to help though  there are times unfortunately where  there are a couple of moments that will  be frustratingly jarring more than once  you're forced to engage in some instant  fail cat-and-mouse sequences that don't  really fit with the overall tone of what  observers trying to create  however they are brief and over within a  few minutes and problems like this are  quickly forgotten when you're lost in a  discussion with a tenant telling you  about his religious order which rejects  body modifications children of the  immaculate hope or slowly discovering  the oppressive extent of Chiron's reach  from desktop computers to picture frames  and that's why observer succeeds as well  as it does every scene as a meaningful  piece of the puzzle to a world and story  that you want to immediately know more  about it consistently presents surreal  moments and surprises that would seem  like on paper the work of lunatics  however in this grimy and hopeless  corner of Krakow they feel completely at  home the writing for even the most  fleeting characters even dead ones feels  genuine every person here from crappy  parents yelling at their kids to  abstract constructs of lost souls  trapped in their own minds has a  convincing life of their own and it's  that commitment to detail that makes  Lazar skeeze descent into his future  hell and his own personal demons all the  more compelling cyberpunk is a  reflection of where we're headed as a  society and oddly alluring reality we've  allowed impressive technology into our  lives at the cost of our own humanity  this is a nice genre that needs new  revisions a new pioneers so we can keep  evolving as we inch closer to seeing its  fictional warnings play out in real life  an observer adds to the familiar  parables and fascinating and unexpected  ways in that respect and on many other  levels observer is a haunting and  remarkable achievement  you

